Campfire for BEAM: an HFT contract tx never runs twice after a wallet restart

DEX trades are "dependent" (HFT) contract calls: each variant is valid at exactly one
block height, and when it misses its block the core re-runs the app shader and builds
another variant (contract_transaction.cpp RetryHft / State::RebuildHft). Before building
one it checks that no earlier variant got in ("waiting prev unconfirm") and that none is
still pending (IsHftPending).

Stock builds persist the invoke data only once, at process_invoke_data
(ContractDataPacked, shaders_manager.cpp:358). A rebuild replaces it in memory only
(contract_transaction.cpp:676). After a restart, Init() therefore pairs the CURRENT
variant's kernel/inputs/outputs with the FIRST variant's parent context. Then:

  * IsExpired() uses the old parent height and can call a live variant expired;
  * IsHftPending() derives the wrong dependent context and cannot see the variant the
    node is holding, while the node's dependent state is not even received yet right
    after HftSubscribe (fly_client.cpp:88-112, node.cpp:3538-3540);
  * RetryHft -> SaveToHftv files the live variant under the old height (and, since the
    tx was moved out before EnsureNewCtx(), dereferences an empty m_pNewCtx for its hash);
  * ConfirmHfts and the rebuild guard skip variants keyed at or below
    KernelUnconfirmedHeight, so the live variant's kernel is never looked up.

Mainnet, 2026-10-07: a small BEAM -> FOMO swap was quit while unconfirmed. After the
restart the core built two variants on top of its own pending one (node: "Inputs
missing" twice), the pending one was mined, its kernel was never checked, and another
variant was mined three blocks later. One swap, executed twice.

This patch makes double execution impossible on that path, and keeps the variant data
truthful:

  1. A rebuilt variant's invoke data is persisted (ContractDataPacked) before its kernel,
     so after a restart the parent context matches the transaction in the DB.
  2. An HFT tx resumed in flight (state past Initial, or any earlier variant) never builds
     another variant (m_NoRebuild). It re-checks every variant's kernel
     (KernelUnconfirmedHeight is reset) and then completes with the one that got in, or
     fails as expired with nothing spent. Stopped between variants (RebuildHft, or Initial
     with variants, or no current kernel) it only confirms the earlier ones.
  3. A registration answer of InvalidInput ("Inputs missing") for an HFT variant stops
     rebuilding too: something already spent its inputs, most likely our own variant.
  4. Heights come from the kernels: a dependent kernel's height range is exactly its block.
     Used for the current variant (IsExpired, ConfirmHfts, the confirm key), for the key
     SaveToHftv files a variant under, and to re-key variants loaded from the DB (older
     builds could have filed them under a stale height).

Trade-off: a swap interrupted by a restart, or answered "Inputs missing", is no longer
redone at a new price. It completes if one of its variants got in, otherwise it ends as
failed (expired) a few blocks later and nothing is spent; the user swaps again. Same-run
rebuilds (someone else traded first, no restart) are unchanged.

Regression test: scripts/beam/core/tests/hft_resume_test.cpp, run by
scripts/beam/core/test_hft_resume.sh (fails on the stock file, passes with this patch).

Applies after 0005-neutral-source-dir-and-android-exec.patch, to tag beam-7.5.14493,
with patch -p1. Touches only wallet/core/contract_transaction.cpp.

